{"id":"fe2a0fcf-c031-42ad-a8b2-f5ebefeffb76","object":"chat.completion","created":1785031973,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    text = case['text']\\n    passes = case['passes']\\n    max_rounds = case['max_rounds']\\n    applications = []\\n    fixed_point = False\\n    for _ in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            old = p['old']\\n            new = p['new']\\n            if old in text:\\n                text = text.replace(old, new)\\n                applications.append(p['name'])\\n                changed = True\\n        if not changed:\\n            fixed_point = True\\n            break\\n    return {'text': text, 'fixed_point': fixed_point, 'applications': applications}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to write `solve(case)` based on the task description. The task is SE-CR-01. The output must be a JSON object with keys applications (array of strings), fixed_point (boolean), text (string). The input `case` is the payload object from the fixture. The payload has fields: `text`, `passes` (array of objects with name, old, new), `max_rounds`, `_case_nonce` (but we ignore nonce). We need to simulate string replacement passes. The task likely: apply the passes sequentially in order, each pass replaces all occurrences of `old` with `new` in the current text, and we repeat the entire process for up to `max_rounds` times. We need to find if the text reaches a fixed point (no change after a full round) and record the applications (the names of passes that actually made replacements in the final round? Or something else?) The output says \"applications\": array of strings. Possibly the sequence of pass names that were applied in the last round? Or all passes that ever applied? Need to infer from context. This is reminiscent of a \"string rewriting system\" where we apply passes in order repeatedly until no change or